Package: Rcausality
Type: Package
Title: Causality Analysis for Time Series
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Zsolt T.", "Kosztyán", email = "kosztyan.zsolt@gtk.uni-pannon.hu",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")))
Description: A unified interface to causality detection methods for time
    series, returning one result object ('causres') with 'print', 'summary'
    and 'plot' methods for two series, a data frame (all pairs) or two
    blocks of series. Implements Granger causality with classical and
    Bayesian (spike-and-slab regression, BIC, g-prior and hyper-g Bayes
    factor) decisions; conditional
    mutual information with local-permutation tests and the lag-shifted
    scheme of Zlatniczki et al. (2021) <doi:10.3390/e23111450>; the
    Markov-chain approach of Stippinger et al. (2023)
    <doi:10.3390/math11040852>; the degrees-of-freedom (conditional
    variance) method of Telcs, Kurbucz and Jakovac (2025)
    <doi:10.1103/PhysRevE.112.014204>; Bayesian dimensional causality of
    Benko et al. (2024) <doi:10.1016/j.chaos.2024.115142>; the
    complexity-based CCDH method of Stippinger et al. (2023)
    <doi:10.1016/j.chaos.2023.114054> and the df-entropy method of Jakovac
    et al.; finite-resolution MAR-PID of Telcs (2026)
    <doi:10.3390/e28060641>; the recurrence-plot criteria of Hirata and
    Aihara (2010) <doi:10.1103/PhysRevE.81.016203> and the
    correlation-dimension relations of Krakovska (2019)
    <doi:10.3390/e21090818>; transfer entropy and convergent cross mapping
    as baselines; an optional wrapper for PCMCI (Runge et al., 2019,
    <doi:10.1126/sciadv.aau4996>) through the 'Python' package 'tigramite';
    tools to compare and benchmark methods,
    causality-informed forecasting, multi-core execution, and a Bayesian
    variant of every method with explicit priors, posterior draws and
    Bayes-factor or posterior-probability decisions.
